---
import MotionPage from '@/components/MotionPage.astro';
import ForFramework from '@/components/ForFramework.astro';
import Code from '@/components/Code.astro';
import MotionStage from '@/components/motion/MotionStage.astro';
import MotionUsage from '@/components/motion/MotionUsage.astro';
import MotionOptions from '@/components/motion/MotionOptions.astro';
import MotionTokens from '@/components/motion/MotionTokens.astro';
import Gallery from '@/components/motion/scenes/Gallery.astro';
import { GalleryControls } from '@/components/motion/scenes/GalleryControls';
import { MotionSharedReact } from '@/examples/react/motion-shared.tsx';
import { MotionSharedAngular } from '@/examples/angular/motion-shared.ts';
import MotionSharedSvelte from '@/examples/svelte/motion-shared.svelte';

const defineHeroMorph = `import { defineMotion, defineShared } from '@udixio/motion';

// Each element bound to this motion holds the key 'hero', so the two elements that share it morph into each other.
defineMotion('hero-morph', { verb: 'layout', shared: defineShared('hero') });`;
---
<MotionPage
  slug="shared-elements"
  title="Motion: morph one into another"
  description="Two elements that share a key are one thing for the eye: a thumbnail opens into its detail, and the detail closes back into it."
  frameworkSwitch
>
  <ForFramework as="span" slot="summary">
    <Fragment slot="html">Give two elements the same <code>data-motion-shared</code> key: when one shows while the other is hidden, it starts from the other's place and size.</Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="react">Give two <code>&lt;Motion&gt;</code> elements the same <code>shared</code> key: when one renders while the other is gone, it starts from the other's place and size.</Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="angular">Bind the same <code>[udxMotionShared]</code> key to two elements: when one appears while the other is gone, it starts from the other's place and size.</Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="svelte">Pass the same <code>shared</code> key to <code>motion()</code> on two elements: when one appears while the other is gone, it starts from the other's place and size.</Fragment>
  </ForFramework>

  <MotionStage scene="gallery" label="Live example: Morph one into another" height={544}>
    <Fragment slot="controls"><GalleryControls client:visible size="page" /></Fragment>
    <Gallery heading="h3" />
  </MotionStage>

  <h2>Morph a thumbnail into its detail</h2>
  <p>
    Two elements that carry the same key are one thing for the eye. When one of them appears while the other is gone, it
    starts from the other's last place and size, and travels to its own. Show the detail and hide the thumbnail in the same
    change, so that the two are in the same moment. The morph moves and resizes the element: it does not cross-fade the two,
    and it does not use the View Transitions API.
  </p>
  <ForFramework>
    <p slot="html">Give the thumbnail and the detail <code>data-motion="reflow"</code> and the same <code>data-motion-shared</code> key. In the click handler, hide the thumbnail and show the detail.</p>
    <p slot="react">Render the thumbnail, or the detail, as a <code>&lt;Motion name="reflow"&gt;</code> with the same <code>shared</code> key. The state that picks one of them is the only change.</p>
    <p slot="angular">Put <code>udxMotion="reflow"</code> and the same <code>[udxMotionShared]</code> key on the thumbnail and on the detail. Show one of them with <code>&#64;if</code>.</p>
    <p slot="svelte">Pass the same <code>shared</code> key to <code>motion('reflow')</code> on the thumbnail and on the detail. Show one of them with <code>&#123;#if&#125;</code>.</p>
  </ForFramework>
  <p>
    The example mounts the thumbnail of a photo, or its detail, and not both: the detail takes the place of the thumbnail.
  </p>
  <MotionUsage name="motion-shared" previewHeight={[296, 280]}>
    <MotionSharedReact slot="react" client:visible />
    <MotionSharedAngular slot="angular" client:visible />
    <MotionSharedSvelte slot="svelte" client:visible />
  </MotionUsage>

  <h2>Give the two elements one key</h2>
  <p>A key is kebab-case, such as <code>photo-1</code>. Give it on each element, in the way of your framework:</p>
  <ForFramework>
    <p slot="html">Give it in the <code>data-motion-shared</code> attribute, such as <code>data-motion-shared="photo-1"</code>.</p>
    <p slot="react">Give it in the <code>shared</code> prop of <code>&lt;Motion&gt;</code>, such as <code>shared="photo-1"</code>.</p>
    <p slot="angular">Bind it with <code>[udxMotionShared]</code>, such as <code>[udxMotionShared]="'photo-' + id"</code>.</p>
    <p slot="svelte">Give it in the <code>shared</code> option of <code>motion()</code>, such as <code>motion('reflow', () =&gt; (&#123; shared: 'photo-1' &#125;))</code>.</p>
  </ForFramework>
  <p>
    A layout definition can hold the key too. <code>defineShared()</code> returns the key as a typed name, and the definition
    is the same in every framework:
  </p>
  <Code data-code={defineHeroMorph} data-language="ts" />

  <h2>Slide a tab indicator with Tabs</h2>
  <p>
    To slide an indicator from one tab to the next, use the <code>Tabs</code> component of your framework. It moves its own
    indicator on the default spatial spring, so you give the tabs no shared key. The filter of the example is a
    <code>Tabs</code>.
  </p>

  <h2>Options</h2>
  <MotionOptions verb="layout" />

  <h2>Timing and tokens</h2>
  <p>A morph moves on the default spatial spring, unless the definition of its layout gives it another timing.</p>
  <MotionTokens tokens={['spring.default.spatial']} />

  <h2>Reduced motion</h2>
  <p>
    Under reduced motion, or with <code>--udx-motion: none</code>, the detail opens and closes at once, and the indicator of a
    <code>Tabs</code> moves at once.
  </p>

  <h2>Limits</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>If two elements with the same key are shown together, only one of them morphs: give the other one its own key. In development, the page reports it.</li>
    <li>If the second element appears more than 600 ms after the first one was hidden or removed, it does not morph: it starts at its own place. Show the two in the same change.</li>
    <li>If the element is an SVG element, binding a layout motion throws: put the key on an HTML element around it.</li>
  </ul>
</MotionPage>
